WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.520
There’s been a strange phenomenon sweeping
central Germany.

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:08.440
While the true extent of its influence is
still unknown, it seems to have been going

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:13.019
on for quite some time now, usually in irregular
intervals.

00:00:13.019 --> 00:00:17.350
If you were to head down to any of the towns
within the affected region for a visit, the

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:21.490
chances of you noticing anything out of the
ordinary would still be rather low.

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:26.400
But then again, if you’re in the wrong place
at the wrong time, it's entirely possible

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:34.070
you could witness an occurrence of SCP-3023
- Every arachnophobe's worst nightmare.

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:39.250
One terrifying incident happened at a baseball
game, held during the height of the summer.

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:43.899
With the scorching sun hanging high above
a stadium packed with eager fans, the home

00:00:43.899 --> 00:00:48.640
team was neck and neck with their long-time
rivals from the next town over.

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:53.370
As the players took to the field after a changeover,
everything hung in the balance.

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:59.399
The home team’s coach had made a bold change,
sending out a new baseman, a young man named

00:00:59.399 --> 00:01:00.399
Jannick Denke.

00:01:00.399 --> 00:01:05.619
He was a rookie, untested, but the team’s
strongest veterans had been doing their best

00:01:05.619 --> 00:01:10.930
through the whole first half of the game,
and still, the scores were almost tied.

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:15.750
And so, Jannick stepped up to the base, unaware
that making the next catch would change his

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:17.430
life forever.

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:22.340
The crowd was silent, the tension flattening
their cheers and chants to a low murmur as

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:24.860
the rival’s heaviest hitter stepped up to
bat.

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:30.270
He was a behemoth, arms twice the size of
the baseball bat he carried over his broad

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:34.470
shoulder, striding up with confidence as he
readied a swing.

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:38.730
Watching and waiting, a bead of sweat rolled
down Jannick’s forehead, dropping down the

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:39.850
bridge of his nose.

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:45.750
He couldn’t tell which was making him sweat
more: the heat of the sun or his own nerves.

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:49.820
His teammate at the pitcher’s mound lifted
a leg, the baseball in hand.

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:53.970
If he’d gripped the ball any tighter, his
fingernails might’ve splintered and got

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:57.210
lodged in the white synthetic leather wrapped
around it.

00:01:57.210 --> 00:02:02.080
Jannick stared, not even bothering to wipe
away the drops of sweat in his eyes.

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:06.170
As his teammate’s throwing arm reeled back
and hurled the ball forward, it felt like

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:08.399
time itself had slowed down.

00:02:08.399 --> 00:02:13.260
The rival team’s batter swatted the baseball
out of the air with an earth-shattering CRACK

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:15.510
that sent the ball speeding through the air.

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:18.790
Jannick dashed to catch it; his mitt outstretched.

00:02:18.790 --> 00:02:23.760
The ball was careening back down to Earth,
like a white and red meteorite, almost moving

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:28.340
fast enough to burn-up on re-entry as it hurtled
through the atmosphere.

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:33.900
Jannick could feel his heart rattling against
his ribcage as every instinct told him he’d

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:35.680
never make that fateful catch.

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:41.310
In a final act of desperation, he leaped off
the ground with every ounce of strength and…

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:46.140
All around him, the crowd exploded with the
thunderous sounds of overjoyed applause.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:50.040
The mighty force of the weighty cork ball
was like catching a punch in mid-air, the

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:52.400
tremors of impact rippling down Jannick’s
arm.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:57.830
He felt that first, before realizing that
the ball was now lodged securely in his hand.

00:02:57.830 --> 00:03:00.220
He’d done it, he’d made the catch.

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:01.320
The batter was out.

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:04.190
But before he could even react in celebration…

00:03:04.190 --> 00:03:05.910
it happened.

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:10.180
His arm recovered from the initial shock of
the catch just in time to feel the lightning-fast

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:13.300
flurry of small legs scuttling over his skin.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:17.550
Barely able to catch his breath, the last
thing Jannick saw was something that used

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:21.330
to be a baseball hurriedly crawling up his
chest towards his neck.

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:26.870
From a distance, his teammates, the fans in
the audience only saw him drop to the turf,

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:31.360
flailing his arms trying to brush off something
crawling over him as it attacked and killed

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:36.069
the young baseman in what had otherwise been
the proudest moment of his life.

00:03:36.069 --> 00:03:40.690
While that might’ve been the first time
anything like this had ever happened, it certainly

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:41.860
wouldn’t be the last.

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:47.690
Now, have you ever passed by an abandoned
building, and felt an urge to look around

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:48.690
inside?

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:53.230
Of course, a lot of us have, but most of us
are smart enough to resist the urge.

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:57.650
But on the very rare times you and your friends
have worked up the courage to explore somewhere

00:03:57.650 --> 00:04:02.260
like this, you’ve probably never found anything
all that interesting.

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:07.280
Then again, you might want to think twice
before sneaking past those ‘Keep Out’

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:08.920
and ‘Condemned’ signs.

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:13.520
Maxi and Iva learned that lesson the hard
way when they gained access to an abandoned

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:14.980
office block.

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:19.259
Maybe they were trying their hand at making
a Blair Witch Project-style amateur found

00:04:19.259 --> 00:04:20.259
footage movie.

00:04:20.259 --> 00:04:23.800
Or they could’ve been dabbling in some urban
exploration.

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:28.199
Best case, there might’ve been a few pieces
of office furniture left behind by the building’s

00:04:28.199 --> 00:04:32.910
previous occupants, something that the removal
company forgot to take when the place was

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:33.980
cleared out.

00:04:33.980 --> 00:04:36.710
The pair of them could’ve just helped themselves.

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:41.090
After all, they needed a new folding chair
for their apartment, and there was one just

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:45.340
sitting there…

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:49.250
Trembling through her stifled tears, Iva’s
phone was shuddering in her hand.

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:54.190
The office had been dark, but she was certain
the shadowy shape that had taken Maxi didn’t

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:55.889
belong to a human being.

00:04:55.889 --> 00:05:00.060
Clamping her hand over her mouth to silence
her terrified breaths, she peered out from

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:04.190
under the desk, pointing her phone’s camera
wherever she looked as it recorded.

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:09.430
Iva could hear the loud tapping of several
metal legs, moving hurriedly around the empty

00:05:09.430 --> 00:05:10.430
office.

00:05:10.430 --> 00:05:15.110
The noise would pause at irregular intervals;
every time it stopped, she thought – no,

00:05:15.110 --> 00:05:17.050
prayed – that the creature was gone.

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:22.780
But just as Iva went to look, she would hear
that same sound: quick, scampering steps,

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:27.340
the kind of movements that feel unnatural
to look at, that are only possible for things

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:29.380
with eight legs.

00:05:29.380 --> 00:05:34.181
Perhaps that made it worse; the creature didn’t
shriek or scream or breathe like you’d expect

00:05:34.181 --> 00:05:36.680
of some awful monster in a horror movie.

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:38.520
But then again, how could it?

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:43.430
It had been a chair when Maxi had walked up
to it, nothing more than an ordinary folding

00:05:43.430 --> 00:05:44.430
chair.

00:05:44.430 --> 00:05:48.169
The patter of metal footsteps stopped again,
this time for longer.

00:05:48.169 --> 00:05:50.650
It had to be gone now, she thought.

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:55.080
She gave it another few seconds, just to make
sure the silence wasn’t broken again.

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:59.479
Crawling out from under the desk, her phone
still in hand, Iva allowed herself to breathe

00:05:59.479 --> 00:06:01.130
a tentative sigh.

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:05.289
Only for that sigh to become a scream as it
lunged at her, the chair’s seat and back

00:06:05.289 --> 00:06:08.759
now the body and maw of an angry arachnid
monster.

00:06:08.759 --> 00:06:12.770
As Iva screamed, her phone caught the whole,
gruesome sight on camera.

00:06:12.770 --> 00:06:15.710
You might be starting to see a pattern emerging
here.

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:19.160
But there’s yet another twist in this multi-legged
tale.

00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:21.580
What if these occurrences weren’t just random
incidents?

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:26.330
Sure, they might fall into the ‘freak of
nature’ category, like so many other anomalous

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:27.330
incidents.

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:31.919
But while it’s unclear exactly how these
particular anomalies come about, could it

00:06:31.919 --> 00:06:37.960
be possible that something – or someone
– is creating them on purpose?

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:42.259
Mobile Task Force Alpha-21 were already on
the scene, in the aftermath of the latest

00:06:42.259 --> 00:06:43.330
incursion.

00:06:43.330 --> 00:06:46.600
The elite Foundation strike team had eliminated
the threat.

00:06:46.600 --> 00:06:51.849
Luckily, it had started life as a phone, meaning
they were able to remotely destroy it, causing

00:06:51.849 --> 00:06:54.620
its electronic components to detonate.

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:57.560
Not before it had killed two Foundation personnel
though.

00:06:57.560 --> 00:07:00.180
Naturally, now came the clean-up operation.

00:07:00.180 --> 00:07:03.490
Gathering up evidence, leaving no trace of
what had happened.

00:07:03.490 --> 00:07:08.850
The SCP Foundation still had little clue as
to what exactly caused instances of this nature;

00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:13.750
a phenomenon they had now designated as SCP-3023.

00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:18.580
All they had to go on was a handful of cases,
and footage recovered from a cell phone that

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:23.580
had belonged to an urban explorer who’d
met an untimely end at the jaws of a folding

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:24.580
chair.

00:07:24.580 --> 00:07:29.160
But speaking of footage, something unusual
had been caught by a security camera a few

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:33.090
days before the latest SCP-3023 incident.

00:07:33.090 --> 00:07:38.231
The security footage showed a man breaking
into an office where the latest 3023 instance

00:07:38.231 --> 00:07:40.630
– the telephone – had been found.

00:07:40.630 --> 00:07:44.900
As he picked up the phone in question, this
individual’s jaw appeared to unnaturally

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:51.250
split open horizontally, allowing four dark,
tongue-like appendages to emerge.

00:07:51.250 --> 00:07:55.479
These appendages rubbed the phone for over
half a minute, before retracting.

00:07:55.479 --> 00:07:59.930
The man then returned the phone to its original
place and promptly left the office.

00:07:59.930 --> 00:08:04.430
Thanks to further investigations conducted
by the Foundation’s forensic experts, this

00:08:04.430 --> 00:08:09.370
unknown individual was identified as a Mr.
Sauer, the owner of a local restaurant.

00:08:09.370 --> 00:08:15.050
Naturally, MTF Alpha-21 moved in to apprehend
this suspect, the only real lead as to what

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:20.720
had been causing the multiple instances of
SCP-3023 to begin occurring in Germany.

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:26.000
However, when Sauer was eventually detained,
he showed next to no sign of any anomalies

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:27.000
in his body.

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:31.129
He claimed to have no memory of the events
depicted in the security footage, had never

00:08:31.129 --> 00:08:37.050
encountered any previous SCP-3023 instance,
and seemed to possess no knowledge of the

00:08:37.050 --> 00:08:39.860
strange properties he'd exhibited on camera.

00:08:39.860 --> 00:08:45.540
Nonetheless, the SCP Foundation was forced
to detain Mr. Sauer, although he never displayed

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:47.890
any anomalous behavior ever again.

00:08:47.890 --> 00:08:52.930
Now, you might be forgiven for thinking that,
with Sauer held in Foundation custody, everyone

00:08:52.930 --> 00:08:55.110
could breathe a sigh of relief.

00:08:55.110 --> 00:09:00.610
But, sadly for any arachnophobes watching
at home, new instances of SCP-3023 kept cropping

00:09:00.610 --> 00:09:05.980
up, in even stranger and more horrific fashion
than ever before.

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:10.120
Imagine you had a headache, and we’re talking
about a real killer here.

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:13.490
One of those “power drill to the frontal
lobe” migraines.

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:17.580
Maybe you’d spent too much time glued to
a computer screen at work, and all that blue

00:09:17.580 --> 00:09:20.620
light from your monitor scrambled your gray
matter.

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:25.900
Or perhaps last night was a pretty wild one,
and after a few too many drinks you were left

00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:28.149
feeling hungover the next morning.

00:09:28.149 --> 00:09:30.880
What’s your go-to response in that situation?

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:35.740
Obviously, you call in sick to work, then
go to your medicine cabinet or an over-the-counter

00:09:35.740 --> 00:09:38.480
pharmacy and grab some basic pain killers.

00:09:38.480 --> 00:09:44.940
Paracetamol, aspirin, ibuprofen, all things
that we trust to make us feel better…

00:09:44.940 --> 00:09:47.170
not to make things even worse.

00:09:47.170 --> 00:09:50.870
To Patrik, this started as one of the most
normal things in the world.

00:09:50.870 --> 00:09:56.180
Like you or I, his immediate response to finding
himself suffering from a raging headache was

00:09:56.180 --> 00:09:59.330
to grab a gelatine capsule of ibuprofen.

00:09:59.330 --> 00:10:04.630
As casually and unsuspectingly as anyone would,
he took the pill in the hopes of quickly relieving

00:10:04.630 --> 00:10:09.840
his pain and carrying on with his day, probably
even chasing it down with a quick glass of

00:10:09.840 --> 00:10:10.840
water.

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:16.311
Only, unbeknownst and unseen to Patrik, something
happened the moment that ibuprofen capsule

00:10:16.311 --> 00:10:19.380
passed through his lips and went towards his
throat.

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:23.160
Something that stopped it from fully going
down his throat, in fact.

00:10:23.160 --> 00:10:27.339
Much like the baseball, the folding chair,
the phone – and who knows how many other

00:10:27.339 --> 00:10:31.850
unrecorded incidents – the pill had sprouted
eight, spider-like legs.

00:10:31.850 --> 00:10:36.830
At first, it started as a gentle cough, like
you’d expect when a capsule gets lodged

00:10:36.830 --> 00:10:38.000
in your throat.

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:41.890
Grabbing a tissue, Patrik gave a few grunting
attempts at clearing his airway.

00:10:41.890 --> 00:10:46.829
There was definitely something in there, that
almost felt like it was scratching.

00:10:46.829 --> 00:10:50.820
Not the kind of scratch at the back of the
throat brought on by some allergies, the kind

00:10:50.820 --> 00:10:55.900
of scratching that caused Patrik to cough
up blood when he put a tissue to his mouth.

00:10:55.900 --> 00:11:00.170
The kind of scratching that he could feel
moving, crawling around in his windpipe.

00:11:00.170 --> 00:11:04.980
Perhaps, if he’d had more time, Patrik could
have raced to the hospital, and had whatever

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:09.740
was clawing its way around his throat removed
safely with that free European healthcare.

00:11:09.740 --> 00:11:14.930
Unfortunately, the thing that the capsule
had turned into just as he swallowed it wasn’t

00:11:14.930 --> 00:11:16.370
that kind.

00:11:16.370 --> 00:11:21.279
Wracked with unimaginable pain, Patrik was
writhing and spluttering uncontrollably, his

00:11:21.279 --> 00:11:24.800
mouth filled with more bile and blood than
saliva by that point.

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:29.350
The scratching was moving, and not down through
his esophagus towards his stomach.

00:11:29.350 --> 00:11:35.310
It was going outwards, burrowing through the
insides of his neck until it reached his spinal

00:11:35.310 --> 00:11:36.310
cord.

00:11:36.310 --> 00:11:41.300
By the time the little ibuprofen capsule-sized
instance of SCP-3023 came crawling out from

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:43.870
the back of his neck, Patrik was already dead.

00:11:43.870 --> 00:11:49.820
Let’s say you were aware of this, of all
these strange happenings; seemingly ordinary,

00:11:49.820 --> 00:11:53.410
everyday objects turning into angry, aggressive
spiders.

00:11:53.410 --> 00:11:57.389
Obviously, the Foundation might want to have
a little ‘chat’ with you about how you

00:11:57.389 --> 00:11:59.020
came across such information.

00:11:59.020 --> 00:12:02.690
But for the sake of argument, imagine you
did know.

00:12:02.690 --> 00:12:05.649
You might think the smart idea would be to
leave.

00:12:05.649 --> 00:12:12.200
After all, SCP-3023 instances are only known
to occur in a specific region of central Germany,

00:12:12.200 --> 00:12:15.690
neatly situated in the middle of Leipzig and
Düsseldorf.

00:12:15.690 --> 00:12:20.550
So, you might then think it’s time to up
sticks and leave that area, maybe even leave

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:22.149
Germany altogether.

00:12:22.149 --> 00:12:24.149
Just hop in your car and drive to safety.

00:12:24.149 --> 00:12:25.570
If only it were that easy.

00:12:25.570 --> 00:12:31.440
A family of four was cruising down the autobahn
in an SUV, just another car on the packed

00:12:31.440 --> 00:12:32.520
highway.

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:37.500
Exhausted after hours on the road, Matteo
and Nina sat quietly up front, making sure

00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:42.269
they didn’t wake their son and daughter,
both asleep in the rear passenger seats.

00:12:42.269 --> 00:12:46.910
The car was picking up speed, about to pass
seventy miles per hour as it gradually carried

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:47.910
them home.

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:50.459
Although it wasn’t going to get them all
the way back.

00:12:50.459 --> 00:12:55.510
The screech of twisting metal woke both sleeping
kids up screaming, their parents equally shocked

00:12:55.510 --> 00:12:56.880
at the sudden noise.

00:12:56.880 --> 00:13:00.520
The car lurched and buckled, like something
had collided with it.

00:13:00.520 --> 00:13:03.019
But this was no ordinary traffic accident.

00:13:03.019 --> 00:13:07.829
Without any rhyme or reason, the front of
their SUV warped itself into the distinctive

00:13:07.829 --> 00:13:13.640
shape of a cephalothorax, while the rear turned
into what looked like an abdomen.

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:18.490
As the car shifted and reshaped around them,
the grinding of metal as auto parts became

00:13:18.490 --> 00:13:25.170
huge metal legs, Matteo, Nina, and their children
were still trapped inside, never to make it

00:13:25.170 --> 00:13:26.170
out.

00:13:26.170 --> 00:13:29.550
But the creepy-crawly carnage wasn’t just
contained inside the car.

00:13:29.550 --> 00:13:34.899
The newly-born arachnid abomination hurtling
its way down the autobahn managed to maintain

00:13:34.899 --> 00:13:36.130
its speed.

00:13:36.130 --> 00:13:39.750
Other drivers swerved and slammed on their
brakes to avoid hitting the creature they

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:43.779
couldn’t even believe was scuttling hurriedly
along the highway.

00:13:43.779 --> 00:13:48.279
Unfortunately, this led to them careening
into other cars, smashing headfirst into a

00:13:48.279 --> 00:13:51.830
pileup that claimed the lives of forty-one
people.

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:54.720
Not that the SCP Foundation would ever admit
it.

00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:58.529
With one of their facilities only two hundred
and fifty meters away, they were quick to

00:13:58.529 --> 00:14:03.240
dispatch an airstrike to deal with the spidery
SUV once it became clear that Mobile Task

00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:05.949
Force Alpha-21 couldn’t contain it.

00:14:05.949 --> 00:14:10.480
Across the board, anything capable of sprouting
four pairs of spindly legs and crawling towards

00:14:10.480 --> 00:14:14.279
you with the intent to kill tends to rack
up quite the body count.

00:14:14.279 --> 00:14:17.670
But dealing with bodies are some people’s
business.

00:14:17.670 --> 00:14:21.360
That was the case for Lukas, a newly-qualified
coroner.

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:25.579
After passing years of training, he was working
with the local police department, performing

00:14:25.579 --> 00:14:29.360
autopsies and examining bodies to help them
with their investigations.

00:14:29.360 --> 00:14:34.529
Sure, it may not have been the most glamorous
profession, but Lukas could sleep soundly

00:14:34.529 --> 00:14:37.470
knowing that he’d never get hurt by a dead
body…

00:14:37.470 --> 00:14:42.211
A John Doe – a body that hadn’t yet been
identified– had just been brought in, after

00:14:42.211 --> 00:14:44.339
police had found him on the side of the road.

00:14:44.339 --> 00:14:48.779
Lukas thoroughly washed his hands, put on
his gloves and scrubs, along with the rest

00:14:48.779 --> 00:14:50.160
of the autopsy team.

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:55.260
He’d sat in on at least a dozen of these
procedures, studied the relevant process and

00:14:55.260 --> 00:15:00.839
techniques, everything had prepared him for
the job of figuring out how someone had died.

00:15:00.839 --> 00:15:04.740
But not even the most experienced medical
examiner could be prepared for what happened

00:15:04.740 --> 00:15:05.779
next.

00:15:05.779 --> 00:15:10.940
Taking the lead, Lukas began by making the
primary incision into the cadaver’s chest.

00:15:10.940 --> 00:15:15.470
It always reminded him of a particular scene
in The Thing¸ where a character’s stomach

00:15:15.470 --> 00:15:20.769
opened up and became a maw of frightening
teeth, revealing them to be the titular shape-shifting

00:15:20.769 --> 00:15:21.769
alien.

00:15:21.769 --> 00:15:26.040
That thought was quickly shaken away when
suddenly, to Lukas’ surprise, the body lurched

00:15:26.040 --> 00:15:28.700
violently on the examining table.

00:15:28.700 --> 00:15:33.740
Not everyone expects dead bodies to be able
to move, and while it might be rare, it’s

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:35.709
also not impossible.

00:15:35.709 --> 00:15:40.300
Any number of things can cause someone’s
remains to move after death: muscles atrophying

00:15:40.300 --> 00:15:44.259
or spasming, the body filling up with gas
as it breaks down.

00:15:44.259 --> 00:15:48.420
Of course, any coroner would expect these
movements to have subsided by the time someone

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:50.449
reaches the autopsy room.

00:15:50.449 --> 00:15:55.649
Caught off-guard by the sudden, violent movement,
Lukas stepped away, dropping his scalpel.

00:15:55.649 --> 00:16:00.630
His panting breath warmed his face beneath
his surgical mask as he stared for a moment,

00:16:00.630 --> 00:16:03.089
waiting to see if the body moved again.

00:16:03.089 --> 00:16:08.050
Certain it would be still now, Lukas wrote
the spooky incident off as just a muscle spasm

00:16:08.050 --> 00:16:10.300
and leaned over to retrieve his scalpel.

00:16:10.300 --> 00:16:13.759
But while he was crouching, he noticed something
strange.

00:16:13.759 --> 00:16:18.149
It almost looked as if there were a pair of
protrusions, poking out from under the dead

00:16:18.149 --> 00:16:19.529
man’s skin.

00:16:19.529 --> 00:16:24.220
Walking around to the other side of the table,
Lukas found two more similar lumps at the

00:16:24.220 --> 00:16:25.550
body’s abdomen.

00:16:25.550 --> 00:16:29.800
Almost as if something was inside, ready to
force its way out.

00:16:29.800 --> 00:16:34.980
Without warning, the John Doe suddenly moved
again on the examining table, only this time

00:16:34.980 --> 00:16:36.209
it didn’t stop.

00:16:36.209 --> 00:16:42.550
Lukas couldn’t believe his eyes, the man’s
face was still, frozen in the same dead expression,

00:16:42.550 --> 00:16:47.850
but his arms and legs were thrashing and writhing
around as if he was somehow still alive.

00:16:47.850 --> 00:16:52.450
Four extra limbs suddenly burst from the sides
of the cadaver, and the now eight-legged creature

00:16:52.450 --> 00:16:56.320
reared itself up, leaping towards a member
of the autopsy team.

00:16:56.320 --> 00:17:01.070
It scuttled and skittered about on its new
appendages, while Lukas watched in horror.

00:17:01.070 --> 00:17:04.539
Blood-curdling screams filled the autopsy
room as he bolted for the door.

00:17:04.539 --> 00:17:08.780
Lukas raced down the corridor; the coroner
dared not look behind him while sprinting

00:17:08.780 --> 00:17:10.720
through the city mortuary.

00:17:10.720 --> 00:17:13.980
Behind him, he could hear the thudding of
the spider’s multiple limbs right at his

00:17:13.980 --> 00:17:14.980
heels.

00:17:14.980 --> 00:17:19.120
Out of the corner of his eyes, right on the
edge of his peripheral vision, he could see

00:17:19.120 --> 00:17:21.760
the mass of legs scuttling towards him.

00:17:21.760 --> 00:17:25.790
Maybe he would get out, run all the way to
safety before the spider was upon him… but

00:17:25.790 --> 00:17:30.490
how can you hope to outrun something with
eight legs, when you only have two?

00:17:30.490 --> 00:17:35.350
The most important thing to remember is that
while any unsuspecting inanimate object near

00:17:35.350 --> 00:17:40.610
you might suddenly decide to become an angry
spider, the chances of it happening are very,

00:17:40.610 --> 00:17:41.710
very low.

00:17:41.710 --> 00:17:46.210
But – especially if you happen to be in
central Germany – those chances are never

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:47.220
zero either…

00:17:47.220 --> 00:17:55.010
Now go and check out “SCP-2086 MAN EATING
BUS” and “SCP-1562 THE CARNIVOROUS SLIDE”

00:17:55.010 --> 00:17:58.900
for more tales of everyday objects that are
far more sinister than they first seem.

